Vendored Brainfuck benchmark programs — provenance and licences
================================================================

These files are vendored verbatim from the matslina/bfoptimization
benchmark suite (https://github.com/matslina/bfoptimization). The
wrapping project (AmazingBF) only uses them for performance measurement
under cargo bench and never links them into the release binary.

Per-file credits
----------------

- awib-0.4.b
  Alexander Kulikov ("matslina"), `awib` 0.4 Brainfuck compiler written
  in Brainfuck. Licensed under the zlib licence (see
  https://github.com/matslina/awib).

- factor.b
  Brian Raiter, http://www.muppetlabs.com/~breadbox/bf/factor.b.txt
  Published without an explicit licence; treated here as informally
  shared public source.

- mandelbrot.b
  Erik Bosman,
  http://esoteric.sange.fi/brainfuck/utils/mandelbrot/mandelbrot.b
  Published without an explicit licence; treated here as informally
  shared public source.

- hanoi.b
  Clifford Wolf, http://www.clifford.at/bfcpu/hanoi.bf
  Published without an explicit licence; treated here as informally
  shared public source.

- dbfi.b
  Daniel B. Cristofani, http://www.hevanet.com/cristofd/bf/dbfi.b
  The author explicitly released this into the public domain.

- long.b
  Attribution in the matslina/bfoptimization repository only; no
  upstream licence. Treated as informally shared public source.

Re-distribution notice
----------------------

If any of the per-file attributions above is incomplete or incorrect,
open an issue on the AmazingBF repository and the file(s) in question
will be removed or replaced.
